    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>h(x,y,z) = xy\frac{1}{z^{3}}, \left(2,-2,2\right), \left(-2,5,2\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(2,-2,2\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-2,5,2\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1.25</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y,z) = \left(2,-2,2\right)</m> to find 
<m>h(2,-2,2) = 2 \cdot -2 \cdot \frac{1}{2^{3}} = \frac{-4}{8} = -0.5</m>.



For the second point, substitute <m>(x,y,z) = \left(-2,5,2\right)</m> to find 
<m>h(-2,5,2) = -2 \cdot 5 \cdot \frac{1}{2^{3}} = \frac{-10}{8} = -1.25</m>.





</solution>
